## Source
2026-06-04 foundations audit: PEP section 10 states "single-threaded
by design ... output ordering deterministic (reproducible list/check,
golden-file tests)"; any future parallelism gated behind an explicit
--jobs flag defaulting to 1. The guard sweep found NO enforcement:
no goroutine guard, no determinism probe.

## Fix
Mechanical-first, two layers:
1. Grep ratchet: zero goroutine-launch statements (`go ` keyword) in
   src/go non-test code -- zero today, so the ratchet starts clean.
2. Determinism probe: build a fixture corpus twice with different file
   creation order, run check/list/ready, byte-compare the outputs
   (and byte-compare across two consecutive runs on the same corpus).
Follow the 0146 negative-control convention for both layers.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Goroutine grep ratchet in make test with negative control
- [ ] Output-determinism probe (creation-order shuffle + rerun) green
- [ ] Negative controls prove both guards can fail
- [ ] make check passes
